 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "In 1980, an oil rig punched a tiny hole into a shallow lake, and accidentally drank the entire body of water.",
   "words": [
    0,
    20
   ],
   "subject": "surveyor"
  },
  {
   "text": "Lake Peigneur was only ten feet deep. But nobody checked what was underneath.",
   "words": [
    21,
    33
   ],
   "subject": "surveyor"
  },
  {
   "text": "Thirteen hundred feet below lay a giant salt mine with fifty-five miners and fifty-foot ceilings.",
   "words": [
    34,
    48
   ],
   "subject": "miner"
  },
  {
   "text": "Up on the surface, the drillers misread their map coordinates by just a few degrees.",
   "words": [
    49,
    62
   ],
   "subject": "surveyor"
  },
  {
   "text": "Their fourteen-inch diamond drill punched straight through the mine ceiling like a pushpin.",
   "words": [
    63,
    75
   ],
   "subject": "miner",
   "nouns": [
    {
     "word": "drill",
     "n": 1,
     "show": "drill"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "At first, it was just a tiny trickle of muddy water dripping onto a miner's hard hat.",
   "words": [
    76,
    92
   ],
   "subject": "miner"
  },
  {
   "text": "The foreman prodded the wet roof, shrugged, and shouted: \"Hey boys, the ceiling is leaking!\"",
   "words": [
    93,
    106
   ],
   "subject": "foreman"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, the freshwater dissolved the salt walls, widening the hole by twenty feet every minute.",
   "words": [
    107,
    121
   ],
   "subject": "foreman"
  },
  {
   "text": "Above, the giant five-million-dollar oil derrick groaned, tilted sideways, and sank straight into the lake bed.",
   "words": [
    122,
    137
   ],
   "subject": "foreman",
   "nouns": [
    {
     "word": "derrick",
     "n": 1,
     "show": "derrick"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Underground, fifty-five miners scrambled onto the elevator as a roaring flood of mud chased them up the shaft.",
   "words": [
    138,
    155
   ],
   "subject": "miner"
  },
  {
   "text": "Miraculously, every single miner made it to the surface before the mine drowned completely.",
   "words": [
    156,
    169
   ],
   "subject": "miner"
  },
  {
   "text": "Now, the lake became a spinning vortex, creating a massive quarter-mile whirlpool.",
   "words": [
    170,
    181
   ],
   "subject": "foreman"
  },
  {
   "text": "It sucked down eleven steel barges, a tugboat, and sixty-five acres of land.",
   "words": [
    182,
    194
   ],
   "subject": "foreman",
   "nouns": [
    {
     "word": "barges",
     "n": 1,
     "show": "barge"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Ancient pecan trees, greenhouses, and docks simply slid into the churning abyss.",
   "words": [
    195,
    206
   ],
   "subject": "foreman"
  },
  {
   "text": "You see, freshwater dissolves rock salt instantly, turning a tiny hole into a roaring underground canyon.",
   "words": [
    207,
    222
   ],
   "subject": "foreman"
  },
  {
   "text": "The suction was so violent, it actually reversed the flow of the Delcambre Canal from the Gulf of Mexico.",
   "words": [
    223,
    241
   ],
   "subject": "surveyor"
  },
  {
   "text": "Creating a one-hundred-and-fifty-foot waterfall\u2014the largest waterfall in Louisiana history.",
   "words": [
    242,
    250
   ],
   "subject": "surveyor"
  },
  {
   "text": "Two days later, trapped air in the mine blew massive geysers four hundred feet into the air.",
   "words": [
    251,
    267
   ],
   "subject": "surveyor"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, like rubber ducks in a bathtub, nine of the sunken barges popped right back to the surface.",
   "words": [
    268,
    285
   ],
   "subject": "foreman",
   "nouns": [
    {
     "word": "ducks",
     "n": 1,
     "show": "barge"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Incredibly, throughout the entire bizarre disaster, not a single life was lost.",
   "words": [
    286,
    296
   ],
   "subject": "foreman"
  },
  {
   "text": "And today, Lake Peigneur is thirteen hundred feet deep\u2014all from one fourteen-inch drill bit.",
   "words": [
    297,
    310
   ],
   "subject": "surveyor"
  }
 ],
